{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CftKPdXy7ZeYTQ26nWLyA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Prioritise fixing bank-connection failures, not streaks and push.**\n\n**Why**\n- Connecting is the strongest lever in your data: connectors retain at 3x. Only 34% connect in week one, and 22% of attempts fail, concentrated at three banks. That is a specific, fixable leak at the point where users get value.\n- The growth team's premise, \"engaged users retain better\", is circular. Streaks target engagement among people who haven't yet got value. Push notifications for an unconnected budgeting app have little to say, because there's no data to alert on.\n- Budgeting is not naturally a daily habit, so 12% DAU/MAU may be closer to the ceiling than a problem.\n\n**Caveat**\nThe 3x is observational. Users who connect may simply be more motivated. The failures give you a cleaner comparison: users who attempted and failed versus those who attempted and succeeded. It's still imperfect, but better than connectors versus non-connectors. I don't know your attempt rate, retry-after-failure rate, or the three banks' share of users, so I can't size the gain yet.\n\n**Six-week plan**\n1. **Weeks 1–2:** Break failures down by bank, error code, and aggregator versus bank-side cause. Look at what users do after a failure (retry, abandon, churn).\n2. **Weeks 2–5:** Fix the top causes. That could mean aggregator escalation or a second provider for those banks, clearer error and retry UX, and a fallback such as CSV import.\n3. **Weeks 4–6:** Add a small, event-driven nudge, such as \"your connection failed, retry\" or a first-week connect reminder. Roll fixes out as a staged experiment and measure week-one connect rate and 90-day retention.\n\n**Defer** streaks. Revisit push once connected users give you meaningful alerts to send, such as balances, bills, or weekly summaries."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3196,"cache_read_input_tokens":5030,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3196},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"52c9fdc7-c267-4df4-86f4-bda76f8949ae","uuid":"8994d01b-6f69-4fec-b02f-220e83168b56","timestamp":"2026-10-10T09:27:04.567Z","request_id":"req_011CftKPdK5abRVWfMwCru6D"}
